# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 7, R2 (`($n + 1) on !go` fires with the tick's opening `$n` plus one) and ch. 8 (a widget function's parameters are its row's; an inlined widget adds no path segment): the click fires 1, the hold of the widget takes it, and `$n` is 1 in the same tick. Equal to the first run, on prismc-f4.
test the_bundle_reaches_the_widget

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="go")
    1: Ui.Label(text="0 0")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="1 1")
